Package: ThermalEV
Type: Package
Title: Analyse LeafSpy Logs to Estimate Thermal Parameters of a Nissan Battery
Version: 0.2.4
Authors@R: c(
    person(
      "Thomborson", "Clark",
      email = "c.thomborson@auckland.ac.nz",
      role = c("aut", "cre")
    )
  )
Description: Implements a thermal model with seven primary parameters, providing routines for importing CSV files from LeafSpy, and for parameter-fitting and plotting. The effective resistance of the pack to charging and discharging currents is the first parameter, in mOhms. When multiplied by the square of the amperage, this resistance gives the "Joule heating" in kilowatts. The second parameter is a polarisation energy, in kJ/V, a cooling factor when the battery is being charged and a heating factor when it is being discharged. Two time constants (in hours) model the pack's equilibration with the ambient temperature, with the second (shorter) time constant being applied when the active cooling system is operating. Two parameters allow a very rough modelling of the active cooling system. The last parameter is theheat capacity of the pack.  
